The independent Go cryptographic conformance implementation uses
golang.org/x/crypto v0.54.0 and golang.org/x/sys v0.47.0. Its complete Go
module graph also inventories golang.org/x/net v0.56.0, golang.org/x/term
v0.45.0, and golang.org/x/text v0.40.0. These modules are copyright The Go
Authors and licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License; their complete license
texts are in ThirdPartyLicenses/.

External GitHub Actions used by CI are recorded in DEPENDENCIES.json and are
not redistributed by this repository.

The independent Swift cryptographic KAT invokes an explicitly selected OpenSSL
3.6.3 command-line tool (Apache-2.0) for Argon2id only.

The protocol key-fixture tests separately invoke the PATH-resolved system
OpenSSL 3 command-line tool inventoried as `system:openssl@3` to strictly parse,
validate, canonically re-encode, and derive the public halves of
software-identity and public-only Secure Enclave identity fixtures. The test
loads that inventory entry and enforces its recorded OpenSSL 3 version pattern
before accepting the provider.

Neither OpenSSL test tool is linked into or redistributed by this repository.

